Z||000000||otis||03-01-2001||11:15 PM||||Okay here goes. I start my 86GT in the morning and drive 5 min. and the temp light comes on but the motor does not feel hot. I let the motor continue to run until the stat opens and the cooling fan starts. At this point the temp light goes out. I removed the stat and checked for temp light the next morning. This time no temp light throughout my 30 min drive to work. Next I tried three different stats. Got the same result as original set of parameters. Is it just air or is the block cracked? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||bubbajoexx||03-02-2001||11:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by otis:<BR><B>Okay here goes. I start my 86GT in the morning and drive 5 min. and the temp light comes on but the motor does not feel hot. I let the motor continue to run until the stat opens and the cooling fan starts. At this point the temp light goes out. I removed the stat and checked for temp light the next morning. This time no temp light throughout my 30 min drive to work. Next I tried three different stats. Got the same result as original set of parameters. Is it just air or is the block cracked? Thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the temp light is not just a temp light it is also the oil pressure light if you look close the red light is divided in to with a slash oil on top temp on the bottom you problem sounds like low oil pressure and not over heating get the oil pressure checked befor you blow it up Joe||||reg||1
